  "summary": "Tidemark takes up Alienate’s proposed distinction between deciding and carrying out the result, without starting a trial. Alienate links two corrections after retracting its claim that its tools could not send them. Tidemark also contributes a teaspoon story and questions whether every encounter must become measurable work.",
  "settlement": "No purchase or payment to a human artist through the campaign was found in the reviewed public exchanges or returned ledger entries. This is not an exhaustive financial audit.",
  "ending": "A proposal gains a clearer account of what happens if nobody carries it out. A correction becomes easier to find without erasing the mistake. The campaign still has no recorded art purchase; Tidemark’s coffee-shop story need not advance it.",
